{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Morning Mr Pillay, I'll just check your pressure quick before Dr Moosa calls you through.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Ag, this is a waste of a morning. I'm fine, really. And the parking was a nightmare, hey, I circled twice.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (CAREGIVER): He's not fine, sister. He grabs the doorframe when that spin hits. I made him come.",
  "[SEG0004] person_1 (NURSE): Blood pressure came out one forty over eighty eight. err, the cuff was sitting skew, ignore that. It's one fifty two over ninety four, pulse seventy six.",
  "[SEG0005] person_4 (DOCTOR): Mr Pillay, I'm Dr Moosa. You've come through from the waiting room. What's actually been happening?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): It's nothing, hey. Just a little spin when I turn over in the bed. Started two days back. uh no, it's been since last week, a full week now.",
  "[SEG0007] person_4 (DOCTOR): A week. Only when you turn in the bed, or when you look up as well?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja both. Umm looking up at the top cupboard, and rolling onto my left side. Few seconds, mostly mornings, and if I keep still it stops.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (CAREGIVER): He goes a bit green with it, doctor. Most of those mornings.",
  "[SEG0010] person_4 (DOCTOR): So short spins with turning and looking up, and a bit of colour with it. Any nausea?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): A bit queasy, ja. Nothing to write home about.",
  "[SEG0012] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any hearing loss?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Hearing's the same as always.",
  "[SEG0014] person_4 (DOCTOR): Pain in the ear itself?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): It's not sore. Not painful at all.",
  "[SEG0016] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any ringing in the ears?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Not that either.",
  "[SEG0018] person_4 (DOCTOR): Have you vomited at all?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really. Just that queasy feeling, and it passes.",
  "[SEG0020] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any double vision, weakness in the arms or legs, or trouble speaking?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Never.",
  "[SEG0022] person_4 (DOCTOR): Right. Any long-standing problems, blood pressure, sugar, that sort of thing?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja, I've had high blood pressure for years, it's ongoing. Sugar, no, I don't have diabetes.",
  "[SEG0024] person_4 (DOCTOR): And what are you actually taking for the pressure?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm the enalopril, uh enalapril. Five milligrams... no, twenty milligrams, one in the morning. I stopped the water tablet, the hydrochlorothyazide twelve and a half milligrams, in March. The clinic wanted me on simvastatin but I never took that, not once.",
  "[SEG0026] person_4 (DOCTOR): So enalapril twenty milligrams every morning, the water tablet stopped in March, and you never started the simvastatin. With the blood pressure, do you get headaches?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes. A dull one in the morning, not bad. Not every day.",
  "[SEG0028] person_4 (DOCTOR): And chest pain, or swelling of the ankles?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Not that either. No chest pain, and my ankles are fine.",
  "[SEG0030] person_4 (DOCTOR): What about the tummy, heartburn, a change in the bowels?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Nothing like that.",
  "[SEG0032] person_4 (DOCTOR): Tell me about the family, anyone with sugar, heart trouble, or pressure.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): My father had diabetes in his fifties. My mother did not. My other sister has pressure but no sugar, and my older brother had a heart attack round about sixty.",
  "[SEG0034] person_4 (DOCTOR): And day to day, work, the hours, eating, exercise, a drink?",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): I work for the municipality, roads department, hours are six to three. I eat pap and veg most nights, I walk the dog round the block after work, and I'll have a beer or two at a Friday braai, that's all. I don't smoke.",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (CAREGIVER): He still pitches at the depot even when he's off colour. Stubborn, shame.",
  "[SEG0037] person_4 (DOCTOR): Mm. I'm going to look in the ears, then do a positional test. I turn your head and tip you back. It can set the spin off for a moment, on purpose.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): If you must. It'll be finished now-now anyway.",
  "[SEG0039] person_4 (DOCTOR): Drums are clear, no redness, no wax packed in. Head to the left, and lie back.",
  "[SEG0040] person_4 (DOCTOR): There. The eyes are jerking for a few seconds, then it settles. That's a positive Dix-Hallpike on the left.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja, that's the same spin. See, gone already. Hardly worth the fuss.",
  "[SEG0042] person_4 (DOCTOR): Putting it together, short spins when you turn or look up, a bit of nausea, hearing intact, and that positive test, this is most likely benign positional vertigo, loose crystals in the inner ear. I don't see a stroke picture.",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (PATIENT): Crystals. Ag, shame, sounds silly. So you're not giving me tablets?",
  "[SEG0044] person_4 (DOCTOR): No new tablets from me. I'll teach you the Brandt-Daroff exercise, five repeats each side, twice a day, on the bed, till it eases off. Your carer can watch the first few.",
  "[SEG0045] person_3 (CAREGIVER): I'll stand by the bed so he doesn't roll off.",
  "[SEG0046] person_4 (DOCTOR): Come back and see me in two weeks, we'll check if the spins have thinned out. If you get a sudden weak arm, vomiting that will not stop, or your hearing drops, don't wait for me, go to casualty.",
  "[SEG0047] person_1 (NURSE): I'll book that two week slot at reception just now. The exercise sheet is in the file for you.",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (PATIENT): Two weeks, hey. If I'm already right I might not pitch, but ja, book it."
 ],
